There is no mathematics on this page. Folio 157v is page 6 of a printed antiquarian bookseller's sale catalogue, section 'Naturwissenschaft und Physik'. It is not a Riemann manuscript.

The page lists second-hand books alphabetically, running from Engelhardt to Guillemeau. Each entry gives author, short title, format (8., 4., Fol., 12.), place and abbreviated year (e.g. 'Leipz. 792/94' means 1792/94). It then gives the binding (br. = broschiert, Ppbd. = Pappband, Hlbldrbd. = Halblederband, Hlbfzbd. = Halbfranzband, Pgmtbd. = Pergamentband, cart. = cartonniert). Sometimes the original price in Thaler follows in parentheses, and finally the sale price in Thaler and Silbergroschen (Sgr.).

Items of mild interest to a historian of science include:
- Euler's Briefe über Gegenstände aus der Naturlehre (trans. Kries, Leipzig 1792/94);
- Erxleben's Anfangsgründe der Naturlehre (several Göttingen editions);
- Franklin's Experiments and Observations on Electricity (London 1751/53);
- E. G. Fischer's Lehrbuch der mechanischen Naturlehre;
- Goethe's Zur Naturwissenschaft and Zur Morphologie (Stuttgart 1817);
- Gessner's Fischbuch (1598) and Thierbuch (1606).

The latest dated items on this page are from 1857–1858 (Garcke, Flora von Nord- und Mittel-Deutschland, Berlin 1858). The previous page includes Crüger, Schule der Physik, 'Erl. 1862', so the catalogue was printed no earlier than 1862. This means it was inserted into or bound with the bundle later, probably used as scrap or wrapper paper. It is unlikely to be part of the 1853 notes proper.

There are no annotations, marginalia or calculations in Riemann's hand visible on the page. A small mark appears in the left margin near the Franklin/Funke entries, which looks like a speck rather than writing. There is nothing to reconstruct mathematically.
